# On layouts/push-out.jsonc an asteroid field of radius 100 lies at (2000, 2000) between two destroyers. Near is ordered
# to a point 5 inside the field's edge, Deep to a point 40 inside it. Each drives in until it meets the field and the
# push-out moves it straight back out by position to the field's radius plus its own model radius. Near then stands
# within tooCloseToTurn of its point, so the push ends its order and it stops where it stands (move=none). Deep
# stands farther off and keeps its order open (move=<x>,<z>): it holds the ring at the same distance from the center,
# without going back and forth, and slides slowly along the ring (a fraction of a unit in 10 s).
# Dumps: "before" shows both 500 from the field's center; "driving" both on their way with move=<x>,<z>; "edge" and
# "later" (10 s on) show both at the same distance from the center, Near with move=none and Deep with its order.
# Run it with --layout layouts/push-out.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
# The points are in the frame of the dump's pos= field, whose z is the layout z mirrored.
wait 1
dump before
select Near
wait 0.3
move 1905 -2000
select Deep
wait 0.3
move 2060 -2000
wait 3
dump driving
wait 30
dump edge
wait 10
dump later
